{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/452457-claimed-what-comes-next","id":452457,"title":"Claimed - What comes next","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-22T03:38:38-07:00","id":452457,"title":"Claimed - What comes next","content":"Hi,<br /> we just had our first session of WtF 2.0. After the troup tracked and killed a claimed Devourer Hound the question came up, what happens to the claiming spirit after the gory (and glorious) death of it's host. Does the spirit die with the host (for spirit and flesh of the living host were merged permanently - and they lost all their health points)? Is the spirit set free immediatly - for the claimed condition ending with the death of the host? Is it immediatly forced back across the Gauntlet - like a manifested spirit which is reduced to 0 health points would? Or does the claiming instantly swith towards claiming a corpse (so the fight can continue twice as gory)? Is it depending on when the spirit releases the Claiming manifestation willingly, even if the host is already dead? Or is the spirit trapped inside the claimed host body until the corpse disintegration takes place? <br /> <br /> My wolfs want to interrogate the claiming spirit - but are very careful about what to do with the dead host body (but this is fine for wolflings as fresh as they are). What do you think? Is there a way for them to kill first, than ask questions? Or did they miss their opportunity to sit down with the Hound, have some tea and talk it out before ripping its head off? <br /> <br /> Maybe it is mentioned somewhere you could point me to? Or am I missing something spirit flowchart wise (which is definitly possible)? Thanks for your thoughts!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5433-zandruin","name":"Zandruin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T08:22:21-07:00","id":452699,"title":"","content":"Hi there,<br /> I know in the 1st edition that having the host body of the Claimed killed releases the spirit, which then suffers a -3 to all rolls for a number of hours due to disorientation (Predators, page 81). But I can't find anything about it myself in either the God Machine Chronicles or in Werewolf 2.0, unless anyone else has better luck.<br /> <br /> Personally though, I would play it as the host body dies and the spirit is released but becomes dormant as if it has lost all of its Corpus. This is because the spirit and body is supposed to be merged completely, so the 'shock' of being released so quickly when the body dies should be enough I think to make it have to recover like that. Hope it's something to consider <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4910,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4910-warrior-angel","user":"warrior angel","date":".  Spelling 03-22-2015, 11:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4910-warrior-angel","name":"warrior angel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4910_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T08:24:13-07:00","id":452705,"title":"","content":"I believe the intent is that the spirit is released when a Claimed dies. A Hive-Claimed is notably different in this regard; the spirits in a Hive-Claimed die with the host.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}